  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far is config_025 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. All four aggregation×fusion combos for scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l have been tested, and scgpt was dramatically worse (0.507). The key unexplored dimension with the proven-best RNA encoder is the image encoder. This experiment tests config_034 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) to determine whether the lighter resnet50 backbone can match or approach ViT-L performance with the best aggregation/fusion pairing. If resnet50 is competitive, it saves substantial GPU hours for remaining experiments; if it is clearly inferior, it confirms ViT-L is essential and we can focus the last 3 experiments on other refinements. Expected relative cost: moderate (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), likely slightly cheaper than config_025 (3.60 h) since resnet50 is smaller than ViT-L, making this an efficient probe of the image-encoder axis."
}

